# Testing Rules — suparship

## Test Categories

| Category | Purpose | Speed | When to Run |
|----------|---------|-------|-------------|
| Unit | Test individual functions | Fast (< 1s) | Every commit, locally |
| Golden | Snapshot output comparison | Fast (< 5s) | Every commit |
| Integration | Test component interaction | Medium (< 1m) | Every PR |
| Smoke | End-to-end demo validation | Slow (5-10m) | Nightly, releases |

## Minimum Test Requirements

### Demo (`suparship demo`)

**Smoke test required:**

```go
// test/smoke/demo_test.go
func TestDemoSmoke(t *testing.T) {
    if testing.Short() {
        t.Skip("skipping smoke test in short mode")
    }
    
    ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 10*time.Minute)
    defer cancel()
    
    // 1. Create k3d cluster
    require.NoError(t, k3d.CreateCluster(ctx, "smoke-test"))
    defer k3d.DeleteCluster(ctx, "smoke-test")
    
    // 2. Run install
    require.NoError(t, runSuparship(ctx, "install", "--profile=demo", "--yes"))
    
    // 3. Verify components are healthy
    require.NoError(t, waitForDeployment(ctx, "argocd", "argocd-server", 2*time.Minute))
    require.NoError(t, waitForDeployment(ctx, "kargo", "kargo-controller", 2*time.Minute))
    
    // 4. Verify sample app is accessible
    require.NoError(t, waitForIngress(ctx, "https://sample.dev.localhost", 2*time.Minute))
}
```

### Renderer

**Golden tests required for every template:**

```go
// internal/renderer/renderer_test.go
func TestRenderService(t *testing.T) {
    tests := []struct {
        name   string
        input  string
        golden string
    }{
        {"basic-service", "testdata/basic-service.yaml", "testdata/golden/basic-service"},
        {"with-secrets", "testdata/with-secrets.yaml", "testdata/golden/with-secrets"},
        {"with-ingress", "testdata/with-ingress.yaml", "testdata/golden/with-ingress"},
    }
    
    for _, tt := range tests {
        t.Run(tt.name, func(t *testing.T) {
            input, err := os.ReadFile(tt.input)
            require.NoError(t, err)
            
            renderer := NewRenderer()
            output, err := renderer.Render(context.Background(), input)
            require.NoError(t, err)
            
            // Update golden files with: go test -update-golden
            if *updateGolden {
                writeGoldenFiles(t, tt.golden, output)
                return
            }
            
            assertMatchesGolden(t, tt.golden, output)
        })
    }
}
```

**Golden file structure:**

```
internal/renderer/testdata/
├── basic-service.yaml           # Input
